## 1. Overview

Tetryonics begins from the observation that squared numbers in physics correspond to equilateral triangular geometries rather than square ones. From this single reinterpretation, Abraham constructs a unified geometric framework that addresses quantum mechanics, electromagnetism, nuclear forces, gravity, chemistry, and cosmology without invoking probabilistic wavefunctions, renormalization, or point particles.

The name *Tetryonics* derives from the **Tetryon**, the fundamental particle of matter in the framework — a three-dimensional tetrahedral standing wave composed of four equilateral triangular energy quanta. Abraham describes the Tetryon as the minimal closed topology that can exist in three-dimensional space, and all observable matter particles — quarks, leptons, baryons, and atomic nuclei — are modeled as integer multiples of this unit.

The theory presents itself as deterministic: given the geometry of the vacuum and the invariant gauge length of 1 × 10⁻¹⁵ metres, all physical constants including the speed of light, Planck's constant, and the masses of all fundamental particles are claimed to follow necessarily from geometric constraint alone, without free parameters.

