## 6. Forces and Their Geometric Origins

### 6.1 Electromagnetism

The electric field arises from the permittivity geometry of ZPF flux. The magnetic field is always orthogonal to the electric field and propagates bidirectionally from the block wall of the ZPF. Abraham derives Coulomb's law, Faraday's law, and the Ampere-Maxwell relation from equilateral ZPF flux geometry. The electromagnetic constants of the vacuum are identified as geometric ratios:

ε₀μ₀ = t_T² / l_q² = 1/c²

### 6.2 The Strong Force

The strong nuclear force is identified as face-to-face equilateral induction between adjacent Tetryon fascia. Opposite-charge fascia attract; same-charge fascia repel. The force range is approximately L = 1.15 × 10⁻¹⁵ m — the side length of a single ZPF quantum — because the contact interaction exists only when faces physically overlap. This naturally explains the short range of the strong force without a separate confinement mechanism.

### 6.3 The Weak Force

The weak force is identified as edge-to-edge inductive coupling between ZPF dipole fields — a lower-energy state than the face-to-face strong interaction. Beta decay is interpreted as a topological rearrangement: when a Tetryon arrangement becomes geometrically unstable, it undergoes a 180° (π) flip to restore 720° closure. The chirality of the tetrahedron produces parity violation. The W-boson (3 ZPF quanta) is the exchange particle carrying the angular momentum flip.

### 6.4 Gravity

Gravity in Tetryonics is not spacetime curvature. The vacuum is a flat equilateral ZPF lattice (Ω_k = 0, proved by the zero angular defect of equilateral tessellation: 6 × 60° = 360°). Three-dimensional Matter topologies displace this lattice, creating a convergent pressure gradient around them. This gradient is gravity:

F = −G × (m₁/c²)(m₂/c²) / r²

which is Newton's gravity with M = m/c² (Matter = mass divided by c²). The 8πG/c⁴ coupling constant in the Einstein Field Equations is interpreted as a two-body interaction (8π = 2 × 4π), where 4π is the single-body tetrahedral closure quantum. Abraham identifies the quantum of gravity as a single ZPF face interaction: hν/c⁴ per face.

